140
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:37,320
I think when I've bought bagels and I say I want a dozen bagels, they give me a baker's dozen.

141
00:06:37,320 --> 00:06:38,320
They give me 13.

142
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:39,320
Okay.

143
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:43,540
So, when you're buying bread, now obviously you don't really buy a dozen sourdough breads.

144
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:46,440
You buy a dozen loaves of sourdough bread.

145
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:49,600
So, the countable noun here is a loaf of bread.

146
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:51,660
One loaf, two loaves.

147
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:56,060
Now, this is very interesting because in English, we don't have that many counting words, measure words.

148
00:06:56,300 --> 00:06:56,420
Right.

149
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,920
But for bread, we do actually have this special word.

150
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:04,480
So, you can say, I would like two loaves of sourdough bread.

151
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:05,240
Okay.

152
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:09,660
And a loaf or loaves in the plural, what is it exactly?

153
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:11,440
It's one big piece.

154
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:15,580
So, for example, you have maybe one little piece of bread.

155
00:07:15,740 --> 00:07:16,340
It's called a slice.

156
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:17,300
That's what you eat.

157
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:20,440
But when you buy the bread, you have many, many, many slices together.

158
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:23,720
Before you cut the bread, that's called a loaf.

159
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:23,880
Very good.

160
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:34,000
And this is the reason why the baker or the person attending the shop asked if he would like to have the loaf sliced.

161
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,120
Would you like the loaf sliced?

162
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:39,460
That means, would you like us to cut pieces of bread from this loaf?

163
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:43,970
Because sliced bread is how you eat it.

164
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:45,400
Right.

165
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:46,400
Exactly.

166
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:48,480
You don't really take a whole loaf of bread and start eating it like that.

167
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:49,370
Like an animal.

168
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:49,650
No.

169
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:50,770
You cut it into slices.

170
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:55,590
So, sliced bread, we say, is one option.

171
00:07:55,960 --> 00:07:59,600
You can also have unsliced, which means when you go home, you cut it yourself.

172
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:04,690
So this is a very particular word as well because you have the adjective to have sliced bread.

173
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:08,740
You also have the verb to slice the bread.

174
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:10,660
That means to cut it into slices.

175
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:14,480
And of course, you have the noun slices of bread.

176
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:16,240
So you have the individual pieces.

177
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:19,440
So it can be a verb, an adjective, and a noun.

178
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:19,580
That's right.

179
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:26,000
