228
00:10:21,080 --> 00:10:23,880
F-L-O-U-R, flour.

229
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:24,850
So there's two different things.

230
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:30,830
There's flours in your garden and there's flour, F-L-O-U-R, which is something you can cook with.

231
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:31,450
That's right.

232
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:33,320
These are called homophones.

233
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:36,490
So they basically have the same pronunciation, but very different spellings.

234
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:37,450
And very different meanings.

